      <h3 id="_specproxy" class="group scroll-mt-20">.spec.proxy[]<a href="#_specproxy" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold">Description</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>ConsolePluginProxy holds information on various service types to which console’s backend will proxy the plugin’s requests.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Type</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><CodeBlock code={"`object`"} lang="plaintext" /></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Required</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <ul>
      <li><code>alias</code></li>
      <li><code>endpoint</code></li>
      </ul>
      </dd>
      </dl>
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Property</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Type</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Description</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>alias</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>alias is a proxy name that identifies the plugin’s proxy. An alias name should be unique per plugin. The console backend exposes following proxy endpoint: /api/proxy/plugin/&lt;plugin-name&gt;/&lt;proxy-alias&gt;/&lt;request-path&gt;?&lt;optional-query-parameters&gt; Request example path: /api/proxy/plugin/acm/search/pods?namespace=openshift-apiserver</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>authorization</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
